<title>GERMANY: ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS WORLD CUP SUPER-G.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS WORLD CUP SUPER-G.</headline>
<dateline>GARMISCH-PARTENKIRCHEN, Germany 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Luc Alphand won the third men's super-G of the World Cup Alpine skiing season on Friday when he clocked one minute 15.32 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Austrian Hermann Maier was second in 1:15.87 with Italy's Werner Perathoner third in 1:15.90.</p>
